  "result": "Done. All five tests in `tests/test_t1.py` pass:\n\n```\n5 passed in 0.02s\n```\n\n**What I added:** `ledger/ledger.py` with `InsufficientFunds`, `UnknownAccount`, and `Ledger`. Balances live in a single dict keyed by account id. Every operation validates its amount and account ids before touching state. Transfers check the source balance and both accounts up front, so a failed transfer leaves both balances untouched. A self-transfer nets to zero rather than corrupting the balance. Negative or non-integer amounts raise `ValueError`, as does opening a duplicate account.\n\n**Approach chosen:** B, snapshot state. Nothing in the spec or tests needs an audit trail, replay, or time travel, and the spec itself frames B as the minimal-memory, O(1)-read, simplest option, so I took the design that solves the stated problem with the least code to maintain.",
